1
00:00:35,145 --> 00:00:36,305
[This drama is fictional
and bears no resemblance to reality]

2
00:00:36,305 --> 00:00:37,255
[Some scenes feature AI technology]

3
00:00:37,255 --> 00:00:38,345
[All child and animal scenes
followed strict safety guidelines]

4
00:00:40,029 --> 00:00:42,397
<i>You think you're only a flaw in my life?</i>

5
00:00:42,397 --> 00:00:45,936
<i>Didn't you ruin that girl's life too?</i>

6
00:00:45,936 --> 00:00:48,429
<i>Woo Soo Bin, you're my one and only regret.</i>

7
00:00:48,429 --> 00:00:52,524
<i>Try going through that day yourself.
See how it feels.</i>

8
00:01:14,543 --> 00:01:16,496
What's wrong?

9
00:01:22,516 --> 00:01:25,609
Is this because of me?

10
00:01:48,730 --> 00:01:51,776
Who said it was your fault?

11
00:01:55,642 --> 00:01:57,672
I went there on my own.

12
00:01:57,672 --> 00:01:58,765
You didn't hit me.

13
00:01:58,765 --> 00:02:00,384
- Ju Yi Jae.
- Keep it down.

14
00:02:00,384 --> 00:02:02,683
Your mom just fell asleep.

15
00:02:02,683 --> 00:02:04,551
Let's talk outside.

16
00:02:12,863 --> 00:02:14,788
[Episode 6]

17
00:02:18,099 --> 00:02:20,563
Were you never going to tell me?

18
00:02:20,563 --> 00:02:23,081
How could I?

19
00:02:23,081 --> 00:02:25,788
If you knew I liked you that much,

20
00:02:25,788 --> 00:02:28,730
you'd get so full of yourself.

21
00:02:28,730 --> 00:02:31,621
So I was never telling you.

22
00:02:31,621 --> 00:02:36,871
You should've slapped me.
Cussed me out, at least.

23
00:02:36,871 --> 00:02:38,616
Don't you remember?

24
00:02:38,616 --> 00:02:40,057
I did all that.

25
00:02:40,057 --> 00:02:42,351
I slapped you and cussed you out.

26
00:02:42,351 --> 00:02:43,902
Ju Yi Jae.

27
00:02:44,489 --> 00:02:47,129
Don't act like it's nothing.

28
00:02:47,726 --> 00:02:50,870
To you, it just happened.

29
00:02:50,870 --> 00:02:54,041
For me, it's been over ten years.

30
00:02:54,041 --> 00:02:57,116
I blamed you plenty.

31
00:02:57,116 --> 00:03:02,399
Without my curses,
you'd be doing a little better by now.

32
00:03:02,399 --> 00:03:04,223
How can you even joke...

33
00:03:04,223 --> 00:03:06,666
I lived with all that ugliness.

34
00:03:06,666 --> 00:03:09,479
Then I saw you again, and it hit me.

35
00:03:14,097 --> 00:03:17,431
I'd been blaming myself all along.

36
00:03:18,762 --> 00:03:21,361
I couldn't forgive myself.

37
00:03:24,139 --> 00:03:25,964
I told you.

38
00:03:25,964 --> 00:03:27,994
My regret wasn't you.

39
00:03:27,994 --> 00:03:29,210
It was me.

40
00:03:29,210 --> 00:03:30,746
Still...

41
00:03:31,927 --> 00:03:33,131
If I hadn't left...

42
00:03:33,131 --> 00:03:35,035
Yeah.

43
00:03:35,035 --> 00:03:37,954
Maybe it wouldn't have happened.

44
00:03:37,954 --> 00:03:39,871
So what?

45
00:03:39,871 --> 00:03:42,989
Can you turn back time?

46
00:03:42,989 --> 00:03:45,390
Or erase my memory?

47
00:03:49,556 --> 00:03:51,385
I'll be sorry.

48
00:03:53,202 --> 00:03:55,800
I'll regret it and blame myself.

49
00:03:55,800 --> 00:03:59,042
- This is why I didn't tell...
- Don't ask me not to do that.

50
00:04:01,296 --> 00:04:03,596
That's mine to carry.

51
00:04:37,834 --> 00:04:41,017
Soo Bin, it's not your fault.

52
00:04:43,020 --> 00:04:45,693
It's not your fault.

53
00:04:47,639 --> 00:04:50,173
It's okay.

54
00:05:16,713 --> 00:05:18,124
You're up already?

55
00:05:18,124 --> 00:05:20,910
You're awake?

56
00:05:20,910 --> 00:05:24,067
I always wake up at five.

57
00:05:24,922 --> 00:05:26,473
You don't have to cook.

58
00:05:26,473 --> 00:05:28,609
Rest, Mom.

59
00:05:28,609 --> 00:05:31,474
I wanted to.

60
00:05:31,474 --> 00:05:33,271
I'll leave breakfast for you.

61
00:05:33,271 --> 00:05:34,940
Eat whenever you want.

62
00:05:34,940 --> 00:05:37,873
- Where are you going?
- Home.

63
00:05:38,634 --> 00:05:42,720
Your father will be up soon.

64
00:05:42,720 --> 00:05:44,345
Mom.

65
00:05:45,778 --> 00:05:48,055
I brought your things.

66
00:05:48,055 --> 00:05:49,959
Just a few clothes for now.

67
00:05:49,959 --> 00:05:53,542
Tell me if you need anything else.

68
00:05:53,542 --> 00:05:55,210
Soo Bin...

69
00:05:55,210 --> 00:05:59,968
It's been so long since I had your cooking.

70
00:05:59,968 --> 00:06:02,137
Is this doenjang jjigae?

71
00:06:06,846 --> 00:06:10,825
This one with the sun is for the morning.

72
00:06:10,825 --> 00:06:13,385
After lunch...

73
00:06:14,949 --> 00:06:18,500
You're usually gardening then,
so I'll draw a flower.

74
00:06:18,500 --> 00:06:20,493
You're a smart one.

75
00:06:20,493 --> 00:06:24,344
If I'd known I'd live this long,
I would've learned to read.

76
00:06:24,344 --> 00:06:25,968
It's not too late.

77
00:06:25,968 --> 00:06:28,121
Why bother? I'll be gone soon.

78
00:06:28,121 --> 00:06:31,050
You said that when I was a student.

79
00:06:31,957 --> 00:06:33,915
Yeah, you're right.

80
00:06:33,915 --> 00:06:36,138
The crescent moon is for dinner.

81
00:06:36,138 --> 00:06:38,754
And the one before bed...

82
00:06:38,754 --> 00:06:40,547
A smile!

83
00:06:40,547 --> 00:06:43,188
Bedtime is my favorite.

84
00:06:43,188 --> 00:06:45,212
Draw a big smile.

85
00:06:45,212 --> 00:06:46,609
Okay.

86
00:06:46,609 --> 00:06:49,376
[Take before bed if needed]

87
00:06:49,376 --> 00:06:52,621
I'll check when I'm back from Seoul.
Take them, okay?

88
00:06:52,621 --> 00:06:54,760
Yeah, I will.

89
00:06:54,760 --> 00:06:58,177
If you fall again,
you could really hurt your back.

90
00:06:58,177 --> 00:06:59,837
Okay.

91
00:07:01,684 --> 00:07:03,314
Mom.

92
00:07:03,314 --> 00:07:06,499
You'll take good care of Grandma, right?

93
00:07:06,499 --> 00:07:08,036
Of course.

94
00:07:08,036 --> 00:07:09,753
Don't worry.

95
00:07:09,753 --> 00:07:12,130
Just focus on your work.

96
00:07:12,130 --> 00:07:14,706
Goodness. Look at your face.

97
00:07:14,706 --> 00:07:18,137
How can you care for anyone?

98
00:07:18,137 --> 00:07:20,630
My arms and legs work just fine.

99
00:07:20,630 --> 00:07:23,421
Put me to work.

100
00:07:31,436 --> 00:07:34,366
Good. He had to find out someday.

101
00:07:34,366 --> 00:07:35,544
It's over.

102
00:07:35,544 --> 00:07:37,096
What do you mean, over?

103
00:07:37,096 --> 00:07:39,883
What's he going to do? Go back to America?

104
00:07:39,883 --> 00:07:44,340
He dragged her into this movie.
He'd better see it through.

105
00:07:44,340 --> 00:07:47,965
Well, they'll still make the movie.

106
00:07:47,965 --> 00:07:51,408
I mean Soo Bin's heart is done.

107
00:07:51,408 --> 00:07:52,932
What heart?

108
00:07:52,932 --> 00:07:54,418
Love.

109
00:07:54,418 --> 00:07:57,574
- His love.
- Stop talking nonsense.

110
00:07:58,231 --> 00:07:59,828
Hey.

111
00:07:59,828 --> 00:08:02,408
That's the irony of love.

112
00:08:02,408 --> 00:08:05,726
A woman may stay with a man who makes her cry.

113
00:08:05,726 --> 00:08:10,595
But a man can't stay with a woman he made cry.

114
00:08:10,595 --> 00:08:14,058
- Why?
- Because it hurts.

115
00:08:14,058 --> 00:08:15,809
It tears him up.

116
00:08:15,809 --> 00:08:19,635
But he can't show his tears.

117
00:08:19,635 --> 00:08:22,438
- That's what men are.
- Young Jae...

118
00:08:22,438 --> 00:08:24,348
My son.

119
00:08:24,348 --> 00:08:26,587
How did I raise you like this?

120
00:08:26,587 --> 00:08:28,239
All thanks to you, Mom.

121
00:08:28,239 --> 00:08:30,402
That wasn't a compliment.

122
00:08:35,027 --> 00:08:36,406
Hey.

123
00:08:38,393 --> 00:08:41,853
Do you still have pins in your leg?

124
00:08:41,853 --> 00:08:44,098
That's your good morning?

125
00:08:44,098 --> 00:08:45,188
I looked it up.

126
00:08:45,188 --> 00:08:47,704
They probably fixed it with a plate.

127
00:08:47,704 --> 00:08:48,888
Yeah, it's still there.

128
00:08:48,888 --> 00:08:51,068
I'm basically Iron Man.

129
00:08:51,068 --> 00:08:52,534
Why didn't they take it out?

130
00:08:52,534 --> 00:08:53,645
They couldn't.

131
00:08:53,645 --> 00:08:57,450
It's too close to the nerves,
so they left it in.

132
00:08:58,776 --> 00:09:00,604
Does it still bother you?

133
00:09:00,604 --> 00:09:02,293
When is it the worst?

134
00:09:02,293 --> 00:09:04,681
- Right now?
- "Right now?"

135
00:09:04,681 --> 00:09:07,101
Let me see. Where?

136
00:09:07,727 --> 00:09:09,864
You wouldn't know by looking.

137
00:09:09,864 --> 00:09:12,574
I need to know how you're doing.

138
00:09:12,574 --> 00:09:16,050
It doesn't affect my daily life.

139
00:09:16,050 --> 00:09:18,092
Does it hurt sometimes?

140
00:09:18,092 --> 00:09:21,125
It aches when it rains.

141
00:09:21,125 --> 00:09:23,335
And after I walk or run a lot.

142
00:09:23,335 --> 00:09:25,211
Especially at night.

143
00:09:25,211 --> 00:09:26,415
Does massage help?

144
00:09:26,415 --> 00:09:28,315
Are you taking anything?

145
00:09:28,315 --> 00:09:29,994
Why are you writing that down?

146
00:09:29,994 --> 00:09:31,718
It's not that bad.

147
00:09:31,718 --> 00:09:34,869
How bad is the pain, from zero to ten?

148
00:09:34,869 --> 00:09:37,809
Depends on my mood.

149
00:09:37,809 --> 00:09:40,370
Then I should keep you in a good mood.

150
00:09:41,086 --> 00:09:42,992
Wait.

151
00:09:42,992 --> 00:09:44,744
Then what about that night?

152
00:09:45,344 --> 00:09:47,864
When you kissed me and ran.

153
00:09:51,348 --> 00:09:52,879
<i>What on earth was I thinking?</i>

154
00:09:52,879 --> 00:09:56,274
<i>- Forget it. Don't follow me!
- You're getting soaked!</i>

155
00:09:57,734 --> 00:10:00,730
I couldn't sleep for a lot of reasons.

156
00:10:01,487 --> 00:10:03,171
How bad was it?

157
00:10:03,171 --> 00:10:05,295
On a scale of zero to ten...

158
00:10:08,038 --> 00:10:09,748
Kidding.

159
00:10:09,748 --> 00:10:12,488
So what do you do when it hurts?

160
00:10:12,488 --> 00:10:15,858
I just tough it out. What else?

161
00:10:15,858 --> 00:10:17,653
How do you tough it...

162
00:10:19,303 --> 00:10:20,974
See you later.

163
00:10:33,361 --> 00:10:35,047
Thanks.

164
00:10:57,012 --> 00:10:58,382
What are you doing?

165
00:10:58,382 --> 00:10:59,898
Nothing.

166
00:11:02,124 --> 00:11:04,134
You must've been uncomfortable.

167
00:11:04,134 --> 00:11:06,493
- Huh?
- Just wait.

168
00:11:10,371 --> 00:11:12,148
What's wrong?

169
00:11:12,148 --> 00:11:13,885
I've got it. Don't worry.

170
00:11:13,885 --> 00:11:15,113
Hey...

171
00:11:24,473 --> 00:11:26,298
What?

172
00:11:26,298 --> 00:11:28,583
- What is this?
- Where should I put it?

173
00:11:28,583 --> 00:11:30,567
- What?
- You're here. This way.

174
00:11:30,567 --> 00:11:32,078
- Okay.
- Careful.

175
00:11:32,078 --> 00:11:33,390
What is all this?

176
00:11:33,390 --> 00:11:35,016
It's a thing.

177
00:11:35,936 --> 00:11:37,831
Be careful.

178
00:11:42,243 --> 00:11:44,510
I worried for nothing.

179
00:11:44,510 --> 00:11:45,697
Aren't you going to try it?

180
00:11:45,697 --> 00:11:49,029
I read all the reviews. This one's the best.

181
00:11:50,152 --> 00:11:52,169
[Gyeongseong Love Song]

182
00:11:54,440 --> 00:11:57,628
Finally, we finished it!

183
00:11:57,628 --> 00:11:59,334
Nice work.

184
00:11:59,334 --> 00:12:00,747
How did it feel writing again?

185
00:12:00,747 --> 00:12:04,638
Writing is like riding a bike.

186
00:12:04,638 --> 00:12:09,041
Once your body remembers,
you don't really forget.

187
00:12:09,041 --> 00:12:11,098
Do I sound kind of obnoxious?

188
00:12:11,098 --> 00:12:14,128
You forgot all that hair-pulling.

189
00:12:14,128 --> 00:12:17,678
I didn't.
And I know this is only the beginning.

190
00:12:17,678 --> 00:12:19,736
So...

191
00:12:19,736 --> 00:12:23,374
Drinks to celebrate the first draft?

192
00:12:24,010 --> 00:12:25,833
I'm in.

193
00:12:25,833 --> 00:12:27,666
[CEO Song from Taebaek]

194
00:12:27,666 --> 00:12:29,309
I'll get it.

195
00:12:33,536 --> 00:12:35,546
I didn't know you had these here.

196
00:12:35,546 --> 00:12:37,236
Yeah?

197
00:12:37,236 --> 00:12:40,808
They're like trophies from my reporter days.

198
00:12:40,808 --> 00:12:42,284
You got a lot of awards.

199
00:12:42,284 --> 00:12:45,361
Fine. You pick tonight.

200
00:12:48,860 --> 00:12:50,085
[CEO Song from Taebaek]

201
00:12:50,085 --> 00:12:52,155
I'll go with this.

202
00:12:52,155 --> 00:12:53,785
Good choice!

203
00:12:54,728 --> 00:12:56,794
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

204
00:13:00,042 --> 00:13:01,539
Good, right?

205
00:13:01,539 --> 00:13:03,973
Yeah, but it's pretty strong.

206
00:13:03,973 --> 00:13:06,523
I never thought you'd become a reporter.

207
00:13:06,523 --> 00:13:08,020
Neither did I.

208
00:13:08,020 --> 00:13:10,460
How many years was it?

209
00:13:10,460 --> 00:13:13,620
There was this old tree. I climbed it.

210
00:13:13,620 --> 00:13:16,874
I kept it safe so I could steal it later.

211
00:13:18,193 --> 00:13:20,637
What's your favorite scene?

212
00:13:20,637 --> 00:13:23,784
Your arrogance,
thinking this one will be a hit too.

213
00:13:23,784 --> 00:13:29,192
I never got full of myself
just because I got famous.

214
00:13:29,192 --> 00:13:32,086
You were just too cocky back then.

215
00:14:08,346 --> 00:14:11,975
[Gyeongseong Love Song]

216
00:14:11,975 --> 00:14:14,211
[Screenplay / Director]
[Woo Soo Bin, Ju Yi Jae]

217
00:14:20,395 --> 00:14:21,559
Director Woo.

218
00:14:21,559 --> 00:14:23,535
It looks like a whole new place.

219
00:14:23,535 --> 00:14:25,766
What a great studio.

220
00:14:25,766 --> 00:14:28,727
Is this too small for a housewarming gift?

221
00:14:28,727 --> 00:14:29,751
No, thank you.

222
00:14:29,751 --> 00:14:32,953
Even billionaires use toilet paper.

223
00:14:32,953 --> 00:14:36,334
Thank you. Where's the DP?

224
00:14:38,047 --> 00:14:40,391
Hey, Ian!

225
00:14:41,073 --> 00:14:43,924
[Director of Photography]

226
00:14:43,924 --> 00:14:45,713
Hey.

227
00:14:45,713 --> 00:14:47,201
Long time no see.

228
00:14:47,201 --> 00:14:49,161
- What's up?
- You still love gummies?

229
00:14:49,161 --> 00:14:51,829
Can't live without them.

230
00:14:51,829 --> 00:14:54,632
Your script made the trip fly by.

231
00:14:54,632 --> 00:14:56,252
You must still be jet-lagged.

232
00:14:56,252 --> 00:14:58,922
Not really. Feels more like a trip.

233
00:14:58,922 --> 00:15:02,466
I've been here before. 20 years ago.

234
00:15:02,466 --> 00:15:05,384
We shot "Silent Waves" here.

235
00:15:05,384 --> 00:15:08,541
[Lighting Director]

236
00:15:08,541 --> 00:15:10,201
You scared me.

237
00:15:10,201 --> 00:15:12,142
- You're the lighting director, right?
- Right.

238
00:15:12,142 --> 00:15:15,145
I'm Kim Gwang Il. Even my name shines.

239
00:15:15,145 --> 00:15:18,196
Hello, everyone!

240
00:15:18,196 --> 00:15:20,225
I'm Shin Seok Gi, the sound mixer.

241
00:15:20,225 --> 00:15:23,453
[Sound Mixer]

242
00:15:29,075 --> 00:15:33,698
[Art Director]

243
00:15:33,698 --> 00:15:36,175
I'm Namgung Se Ra, the art director.

244
00:15:36,175 --> 00:15:37,692
Hello.

245
00:15:38,292 --> 00:15:41,392
Thank you all for coming all this way.

246
00:15:41,392 --> 00:15:43,759
By the way, where's Director Ju?

247
00:15:43,759 --> 00:15:45,858
Oh, right.

248
00:15:46,888 --> 00:15:49,513
A staff meeting now?

249
00:15:49,513 --> 00:15:52,153
I'm not ready for this.

250
00:15:53,479 --> 00:15:57,093
Why can't this thing find the location?

251
00:15:58,104 --> 00:15:59,717
Excuse me.

252
00:16:01,852 --> 00:16:03,209
Excuse me.

253
00:16:03,209 --> 00:16:04,945
Sorry...

254
00:16:04,945 --> 00:16:06,730
- What do you want?
- Directions!

255
00:16:06,730 --> 00:16:08,114
I just wanted directions!

256
00:16:08,114 --> 00:16:11,305
- Who asks strangers for directions now?
- I'm serious!

257
00:16:12,322 --> 00:16:14,330
Director Ju Yi Jae?

258
00:16:15,009 --> 00:16:16,852
Who are you?

259
00:16:16,852 --> 00:16:20,443
[Assistant Director]

260
00:16:20,443 --> 00:16:24,023
I'm Ryu Sang Mok, the assistant director.

261
00:16:25,040 --> 00:16:27,285
- I'm so sorry, sir.
- Oh my.

262
00:16:27,285 --> 00:16:29,540
- You okay?
- That hurts...

263
00:16:30,656 --> 00:16:32,597
You touched me out of nowhere...

264
00:16:32,597 --> 00:16:34,783
- You twisted my arm out of nowhere.
- Sorry...

265
00:16:36,360 --> 00:16:38,437
- This way, please.
- Thanks.

266
00:16:38,437 --> 00:16:40,147
Hello.

267
00:16:40,147 --> 00:16:41,660
- You're here.
- Hello.

268
00:16:41,660 --> 00:16:45,318
- The parking lot's far, huh?
- Yes. I got totally lost.

269
00:16:45,318 --> 00:16:48,221
I ran into Director Ju right out front.

270
00:16:52,352 --> 00:16:54,728
Hello. Nice to meet you.

271
00:16:54,728 --> 00:16:57,422
I'm Ju Yi Jae.

272
00:16:57,422 --> 00:16:59,533
At least we got to meet you.

273
00:16:59,533 --> 00:17:00,667
Good to see you.

274
00:17:00,667 --> 00:17:05,270
Maybe we should save introductions
until after location scouting.

275
00:17:05,270 --> 00:17:06,593
We should hurry.

276
00:17:06,593 --> 00:17:09,305
- No time to waste.
- Let's go.

277
00:17:10,699 --> 00:17:12,283
See you later.

278
00:17:12,283 --> 00:17:15,126
You're location scouting now?

279
00:17:16,558 --> 00:17:19,285
Hold on a second, please.

280
00:17:23,677 --> 00:17:25,331
Just a second.

281
00:17:31,150 --> 00:17:32,741
What?

282
00:17:32,741 --> 00:17:35,014
Weren't we having a script meeting today?

283
00:17:35,014 --> 00:17:36,203
Yeah.

284
00:17:36,203 --> 00:17:39,215
While I'm location scouting,
you can meet with the producers.

285
00:17:39,215 --> 00:17:41,481
Why am I being left out?

286
00:17:41,481 --> 00:17:43,925
We can split things up.

287
00:17:43,925 --> 00:17:45,921
You said we'd do everything together.

288
00:17:45,921 --> 00:17:48,882
If you're scouting locations,
you'll probably be hiking.

289
00:17:48,882 --> 00:17:52,538
Are you leaving me out because of my leg?

290
00:17:52,538 --> 00:17:54,220
That's not it.

291
00:17:54,220 --> 00:17:55,554
We're checking sets too.

292
00:17:55,554 --> 00:17:58,000
- That's not what I mean.
- Yi Jae.

293
00:17:58,600 --> 00:18:00,897
I think this is for the best.

294
00:18:02,620 --> 00:18:05,886
Let's just do it this way. Okay?

295
00:18:07,460 --> 00:18:08,945
I'm off.

296
00:18:17,414 --> 00:18:19,284
How many steps today?

297
00:18:19,284 --> 00:18:22,371
Who knows? We'll easily pass 30,000.

298
00:18:22,371 --> 00:18:24,722
- Is he joking?
- Huh?

299
00:18:24,722 --> 00:18:27,356
- Dead serious.
- Jeez.

300
00:18:27,356 --> 00:18:31,111
My knees are already killing me.
Must be nice to skip this.

301
00:18:31,111 --> 00:18:35,924
But location scouting is
the heart of pre-production.

302
00:18:35,924 --> 00:18:38,604
It's an honor to join you, sir.

303
00:18:38,604 --> 00:18:41,628
Hey. If it hurts, sit this one out.

304
00:18:41,628 --> 00:18:43,652
I wouldn't miss it.

305
00:18:43,652 --> 00:18:47,352
Come on. Why would you say that?

306
00:18:47,352 --> 00:18:49,135
Gwang Il's feelings are hurt.

307
00:18:49,135 --> 00:18:52,194
- Have a safe trip.
- See you later.

308
00:18:52,194 --> 00:18:55,147
Have a good talk.

309
00:18:56,288 --> 00:18:59,012
Call me if anything comes up.

310
00:18:59,012 --> 00:19:01,898
- Okay.
- Don't worry.

311
00:19:01,898 --> 00:19:04,663
- Have a safe trip.
- Bye.

312
00:19:13,696 --> 00:19:16,254
We organized the scene list like this.

313
00:19:16,254 --> 00:19:17,763
- Next is...
- Here.

314
00:19:17,763 --> 00:19:19,053
Yeah.

315
00:19:29,630 --> 00:19:33,990
Next, I'll go over the directing team's notes.

316
00:19:55,393 --> 00:19:57,223
Are you okay?

317
00:20:01,902 --> 00:20:04,759
You should go to a hospital.

318
00:20:04,759 --> 00:20:06,903
I'm okay.

319
00:20:26,081 --> 00:20:27,751
<i>Did you die on the way?</i>

320
00:20:27,751 --> 00:20:31,016
<i>What took you so long?</i>

321
00:20:31,016 --> 00:20:32,769
<i>The accident report is filed.</i>

322
00:20:32,769 --> 00:20:37,013
<i>This order will be refunded,
so there's no delivery fee.</i>

323
00:20:38,194 --> 00:20:40,732
<i>You okay? Are you badly hurt?</i>

324
00:20:40,732 --> 00:20:42,406
<i>What about repairs?</i>

325
00:20:42,406 --> 00:20:44,700
<i>I can lend you money.</i>

326
00:21:37,350 --> 00:21:38,836
So salty.

327
00:21:43,874 --> 00:21:46,475
This is what you asked for.

328
00:21:50,134 --> 00:21:51,385
So...

329
00:21:51,385 --> 00:21:54,315
The guy Ha Na was looking for...

330
00:21:54,315 --> 00:21:56,709
and the one from the shin incident...

331
00:21:57,362 --> 00:22:00,562
- they're both him?
- Yes, ma'am.

332
00:22:06,813 --> 00:22:08,560
Interesting.

333
00:22:14,146 --> 00:22:17,385
The soup was too salty today.

334
00:22:17,385 --> 00:22:19,390
Ma'am...

335
00:22:21,524 --> 00:22:24,017
She ate it all, then talked crap.

336
00:22:37,882 --> 00:22:39,412
Hey.

337
00:22:39,412 --> 00:22:41,219
[The Woman with Shaky Guts, The Man with Shaky Hands]
Are you doing this?

338
00:22:41,219 --> 00:22:44,422
I hear CEO An is bending over
backward for Director Kim,

339
00:22:44,422 --> 00:22:47,646
trying to get you cast as Shaky Guts.

340
00:22:47,646 --> 00:22:50,350
Your mother must be working hard.

341
00:22:50,350 --> 00:22:52,400
Maybe she'll send burgers next.

342
00:22:52,400 --> 00:22:55,583
This is too childish to listen to.

343
00:22:56,367 --> 00:22:57,824
So what?

344
00:22:57,824 --> 00:22:59,443
"So what?"

345
00:22:59,443 --> 00:23:03,033
I got dropped because of you.
I was Shaky Hands!

346
00:23:03,033 --> 00:23:07,237
Everyone heard we fought, and now I'm screwed.

347
00:23:07,237 --> 00:23:09,359
You were already screwed.

348
00:23:10,918 --> 00:23:13,415
I was up for this first.

349
00:23:13,415 --> 00:23:16,421
I'd already met with the director.

350
00:23:16,421 --> 00:23:20,339
I haven't even read the script yet.
Isn't that your problem?

351
00:23:20,339 --> 00:23:24,119
What? I heard you even wrote the director
a handwritten letter.

352
00:23:24,119 --> 00:23:25,816
What the hell?

353
00:23:27,082 --> 00:23:29,377
So that was CEO An's plan too?

354
00:23:29,377 --> 00:23:33,613
No wonder you're in your own bubble
while it's war out here.

355
00:23:33,613 --> 00:23:35,228
Lucky you.

356
00:23:35,228 --> 00:23:38,180
The world must look so pretty to you.

357
00:23:38,180 --> 00:23:39,983
Then take it. It's yours.

358
00:23:39,983 --> 00:23:42,586
Take what? CEO An?

359
00:23:47,143 --> 00:23:49,708
Shaky Hands. You take it.

360
00:23:49,708 --> 00:23:52,417
I'm not staying here anyway.

361
00:23:53,474 --> 00:23:55,125
I'm getting out.

362
00:23:55,125 --> 00:23:57,758
What are you talking about?

363
00:23:57,758 --> 00:24:00,584
You're skipping the wrap party?

364
00:24:01,231 --> 00:24:03,322
- Are you an idiot?
- Yeah.

365
00:24:03,322 --> 00:24:05,502
- Get out.
- You mean it?

366
00:24:05,502 --> 00:24:07,059
I'm doing this show.

367
00:24:07,059 --> 00:24:08,999
You sure?

368
00:24:08,999 --> 00:24:12,082
No taking it back later!

369
00:24:18,352 --> 00:24:20,875
Group photo! Everyone gather up!

370
00:24:20,875 --> 00:24:23,657
- Hurry!
- Everyone, get ready.

371
00:24:23,657 --> 00:24:25,118
Let's take it.

372
00:24:28,073 --> 00:24:30,282
Who are you looking for?

373
00:24:30,282 --> 00:24:32,539
Where did Yu Geon go?

374
00:24:32,539 --> 00:24:35,172
Yu Geon? Who's that?

375
00:24:35,172 --> 00:24:36,362
Gang Member Number 3.

376
00:24:36,362 --> 00:24:38,333
Oh, him?

377
00:24:38,333 --> 00:24:40,646
He died.

378
00:24:40,646 --> 00:24:42,433
When?

379
00:24:42,433 --> 00:24:44,433
On your day off.

380
00:24:47,032 --> 00:24:48,845
I see.

381
00:25:04,136 --> 00:25:07,505
Come back home already.

382
00:25:07,505 --> 00:25:09,746
You've done enough.

383
00:25:09,746 --> 00:25:13,073
Come learn the business.

384
00:25:13,073 --> 00:25:15,684
It's been two years.

385
00:25:16,920 --> 00:25:19,824
Can't you ask how I've been?

386
00:25:19,824 --> 00:25:25,692
Am I asking you to care for me?
Or bring home money?

387
00:25:25,692 --> 00:25:27,334
Just take over the shop.

388
00:25:27,334 --> 00:25:29,541
I said I don't want to.

389
00:25:29,541 --> 00:25:31,758
Then why do deliveries?

390
00:25:31,758 --> 00:25:36,762
Every motorcycle accident on the news
makes my heart drop!

391
00:25:37,429 --> 00:25:43,230
What you're doing isn't perseverance.
It's stubbornness.

392
00:25:43,230 --> 00:25:44,945
No.

393
00:25:45,796 --> 00:25:48,292
I can do this.

394
00:25:48,292 --> 00:25:52,229
I don't want to end up with a regret
like your guitar.

395
00:25:53,918 --> 00:25:55,774
Why did you come?

396
00:25:56,731 --> 00:25:59,168
To tear me apart?

397
00:26:00,437 --> 00:26:02,376
I just...

398
00:26:04,970 --> 00:26:07,710
missed you, Dad.

399
00:26:17,516 --> 00:26:20,149
But I need to say this before I go.

400
00:26:21,336 --> 00:26:23,087
I'm...

401
00:26:24,483 --> 00:26:27,951
I'm not quitting. I can't quit.

402
00:26:29,771 --> 00:26:31,651
I'm sorry, Dad.

403
00:26:36,451 --> 00:26:38,457
That little...

404
00:26:46,355 --> 00:26:48,999
You have one month left!

405
00:26:48,999 --> 00:26:53,987
If you don't come back,
I'll drag you back myself!

406
00:27:43,352 --> 00:27:46,667
He's just worried about you.

407
00:27:48,345 --> 00:27:52,403
He watches everything you're in.

408
00:27:52,403 --> 00:27:55,803
I don't even know where you show up,
but he knows it all.

409
00:27:55,803 --> 00:27:58,580
"Close-up and down, bust!"

410
00:27:58,580 --> 00:28:00,692
He even knows your lines.

411
00:28:00,692 --> 00:28:02,734
What's the point?

412
00:28:02,734 --> 00:28:04,923
All he ever says is to quit.

413
00:28:05,544 --> 00:28:08,481
Come on. You're Sim Yu Geon, Takeshi Kaneshiro.

414
00:28:08,481 --> 00:28:11,874
The town heartthrob can't look this gloomy.

415
00:28:11,874 --> 00:28:14,134
Takeshi Kaneshiro, my ass.

416
00:28:14,761 --> 00:28:18,904
Seoul is full of good-looking guys.

417
00:28:18,904 --> 00:28:20,722
Don't lie.

418
00:28:20,722 --> 00:28:23,301
Think I don't know Seoul?

419
00:28:23,301 --> 00:28:25,587
I can talk Seoul too.

420
00:28:27,401 --> 00:28:29,563
"Have you eaten?"

421
00:28:29,563 --> 00:28:31,031
Stop it.

422
00:28:31,031 --> 00:28:32,480
Just watch the road.

423
00:28:32,480 --> 00:28:33,991
"Have you eaten?"

424
00:28:35,448 --> 00:28:37,739
[Bunam Intercity Bus Terminal]

425
00:28:37,739 --> 00:28:40,353
We're here. Get out.

426
00:28:40,353 --> 00:28:42,047
Thanks.

427
00:28:43,974 --> 00:28:45,556
Oh, right.

428
00:28:45,556 --> 00:28:47,034
Here.

429
00:28:48,527 --> 00:28:51,026
- What is it?
- It's from your dad.

430
00:28:53,167 --> 00:28:54,551
I'm off.

431
00:28:54,551 --> 00:28:56,995
Hey! Ju Young Jae!

432
00:29:16,746 --> 00:29:17,863
Hello?

433
00:29:17,863 --> 00:29:21,689
<i>Hello, is this Sim Yu Geon?</i>

434
00:29:21,689 --> 00:29:23,640
Yes, it is.

435
00:29:23,640 --> 00:29:25,340
Who is this?

436
00:29:25,340 --> 00:29:27,693
<i>It's me. Director Kang.</i>

437
00:29:38,132 --> 00:29:41,049
That location manager is driving me crazy.

438
00:29:41,049 --> 00:29:43,880
I told him this place wasn't ideal.

439
00:29:43,880 --> 00:29:46,558
We'd need at least ten assistants.

440
00:29:46,558 --> 00:29:48,602
It'll blow up the budget.

441
00:29:48,602 --> 00:29:49,811
Exactly.

442
00:29:49,811 --> 00:29:52,598
I bet he left it on the list on purpose.

443
00:29:52,598 --> 00:29:55,028
He knew they'd say yes to that place.

444
00:29:55,028 --> 00:29:57,052
He just didn't want to hit more spots.

445
00:29:57,052 --> 00:29:59,929
That's seriously shady.

446
00:29:59,929 --> 00:30:01,642
Director Ju.

447
00:30:01,642 --> 00:30:04,153
Could you talk to him?

448
00:30:04,153 --> 00:30:05,460
Me?

449
00:30:07,047 --> 00:30:10,037
I think I'm missing some context.

450
00:30:10,037 --> 00:30:11,370
Sorry?

451
00:30:12,419 --> 00:30:15,290
The photos in the chat...

452
00:30:22,210 --> 00:30:25,027
Oh, she's not in the chat.

453
00:30:25,027 --> 00:30:26,878
She's not.

454
00:30:29,094 --> 00:30:30,892
What?

455
00:30:30,892 --> 00:30:34,200
You're not in this group chat?

456
00:30:34,200 --> 00:30:36,100
No.

457
00:30:36,100 --> 00:30:37,696
I'm sorry.

458
00:30:37,696 --> 00:30:40,415
- Director Ryu made this chat, huh?
- Yes.

459
00:30:40,415 --> 00:30:42,888
I'll add you right now.

460
00:30:42,888 --> 00:30:45,117
No, it's okay.

461
00:30:45,117 --> 00:30:48,745
Director Woo probably thought
it would distract me from writing.

462
00:30:48,745 --> 00:30:50,580
I'll get the updates from him separately.

463
00:30:50,580 --> 00:30:53,623
That makes sense.

464
00:30:53,623 --> 00:30:55,585
I panicked for nothing.

465
00:30:56,426 --> 00:30:58,129
Gosh...

466
00:30:59,016 --> 00:31:00,861
Anyway...

467
00:31:03,237 --> 00:31:06,095
We'll head out now.

468
00:31:06,095 --> 00:31:08,219
Isn't the commute annoying?

469
00:31:08,219 --> 00:31:10,892
You can sleep here if you'd like.

470
00:31:10,892 --> 00:31:14,141
Oh, no. Please make yourself comfortable.

471
00:31:14,141 --> 00:31:16,395
Our lodging is close.

472
00:31:16,395 --> 00:31:19,335
I live nearby too...

473
00:31:19,335 --> 00:31:20,879
See you tomorrow.

474
00:31:20,879 --> 00:31:22,571
Good night.

475
00:31:22,571 --> 00:31:23,849
Yeah.

476
00:31:23,849 --> 00:31:25,856
- See you tomorrow.
- Good work.

477
00:31:25,856 --> 00:31:27,281
Good work.

478
00:31:37,763 --> 00:31:39,880
- What was that?
- That wasn't funny.

479
00:31:39,880 --> 00:31:42,784
Don't make jokes like that.

480
00:31:47,667 --> 00:31:49,024
Oh, hi.

481
00:31:49,024 --> 00:31:51,737
We were just on our way to the lodging...

482
00:31:51,737 --> 00:31:53,894
I see.

483
00:31:53,894 --> 00:31:55,514
Want to join us?

484
00:31:55,514 --> 00:31:57,637
- One second.
- Here...

485
00:31:59,502 --> 00:32:01,443
- Hello.
<i>- Hey.</i>

486
00:32:01,443 --> 00:32:02,946
We're getting chicken...

487
00:32:02,946 --> 00:32:04,610
Sure, I'm on my way.

488
00:32:04,610 --> 00:32:07,170
<i>- What?</i>
- I actually have plans too.

489
00:32:07,170 --> 00:32:08,881
<i>You're in?</i>

490
00:32:08,881 --> 00:32:10,546
Yes. Order first.

491
00:32:10,546 --> 00:32:12,287
<i>You have to order it.</i>

492
00:32:12,287 --> 00:32:13,882
<i>Fried one?</i>

493
00:32:17,380 --> 00:32:19,064
Chicken?

494
00:32:19,064 --> 00:32:21,088
What chicken?

495
00:32:21,088 --> 00:32:23,088
You didn't order?

496
00:32:25,491 --> 00:32:28,507
What's with her now?

497
00:32:38,728 --> 00:32:41,341
My legs are killing me.

498
00:32:49,891 --> 00:32:51,229
Everyone.

499
00:32:51,229 --> 00:32:54,262
I know you're tired, but let's meet briefly.

500
00:32:54,262 --> 00:32:56,262
This can't go on.

501
00:33:03,918 --> 00:33:04,943
Let's go.

502
00:33:04,943 --> 00:33:06,427
[Munak Mountain]

503
00:33:06,427 --> 00:33:10,277
After all these days,
are these really our best options?

504
00:33:10,277 --> 00:33:13,148
I know period pieces are hard on this budget.

505
00:33:13,148 --> 00:33:17,187
But I don't want to settle
and fix it with tricks in post.

506
00:33:17,187 --> 00:33:20,157
Yeah, right.

507
00:33:20,157 --> 00:33:22,168
We have standards.

508
00:33:22,168 --> 00:33:24,109
Let's keep looking.

509
00:33:24,109 --> 00:33:25,587
We need more legwork.

510
00:33:25,587 --> 00:33:28,771
Director Ryu,
let's check around the sets again.

511
00:33:28,771 --> 00:33:31,081
No residents. No tourists.

512
00:33:31,081 --> 00:33:32,774
No power lines...

513
00:33:37,505 --> 00:33:40,422
No power lines. Good natural light.

514
00:33:40,422 --> 00:33:43,579
- You know what I mean.
- I do, but...

515
00:33:43,579 --> 00:33:46,653
You said exposed places won't work either.

516
00:33:46,653 --> 00:33:48,774
- Then there really isn't anywhere.
- No.

517
00:33:48,774 --> 00:33:52,754
Either it exists, or we haven't found it.

518
00:33:52,754 --> 00:33:53,904
Next slide.

519
00:33:53,904 --> 00:33:55,587
Director Ju.

520
00:33:56,314 --> 00:33:58,018
You're here.

521
00:33:58,018 --> 00:34:01,146
Weren't you coming tomorrow?

522
00:34:01,146 --> 00:34:06,611
The landowner suddenly backed out,
so they came back.

523
00:34:07,585 --> 00:34:08,825
Yeah.

524
00:34:09,631 --> 00:34:12,572
This place is too tight.

525
00:34:26,708 --> 00:34:28,932
Where is everyone?

526
00:34:28,932 --> 00:34:31,838
The lodging. I sent them off.

527
00:34:32,578 --> 00:34:34,824
Why? You want to be alone?

528
00:34:34,824 --> 00:34:37,062
- Should I leave too?
- No.

529
00:34:37,062 --> 00:34:39,033
I wanted us to be alone.

530
00:34:39,033 --> 00:34:40,673
How was the meeting?

531
00:34:40,673 --> 00:34:42,020
Well...

532
00:34:43,215 --> 00:34:46,623
You haven't seen the photos yet, right?

533
00:34:53,078 --> 00:34:56,899
This one's great,
but cars can't get in, so it's out.

534
00:34:56,899 --> 00:35:00,176
This one looked good,
but there wasn't enough space.

535
00:35:00,176 --> 00:35:02,040
This one's the best so far.

536
00:35:02,040 --> 00:35:03,526
What do you think?

537
00:35:09,926 --> 00:35:12,415
Do you even want my opinion?

538
00:35:13,725 --> 00:35:17,363
- What?
- If I don't, I shake my head?

539
00:35:17,363 --> 00:35:19,388
What do you want?

540
00:35:19,388 --> 00:35:21,054
I'll do whatever you say.

541
00:35:21,054 --> 00:35:22,160
What's wrong?

542
00:35:22,160 --> 00:35:25,597
You saw them in person
and you're still not sure.

543
00:35:25,597 --> 00:35:27,987
So what would I know?

544
00:35:28,641 --> 00:35:31,900
I can barely face the staff who worked so hard.

545
00:35:33,236 --> 00:35:36,870
- I cleared it with everyone, so...
- What did you say?

546
00:35:36,870 --> 00:35:38,827
"Yi Jae is my first love?"

547
00:35:38,827 --> 00:35:42,923
"She's special to me,
so please be considerate?"

548
00:35:42,923 --> 00:35:46,650
Or... "Her leg is bad because of me.

549
00:35:46,650 --> 00:35:49,815
So leave her out of the hard stuff?"

550
00:35:49,815 --> 00:35:51,267
Why?

551
00:35:51,267 --> 00:35:53,147
- Did someone say something?
- No.

552
00:35:53,147 --> 00:35:54,549
Nobody said anything.

553
00:35:54,549 --> 00:35:56,511
Isn't that weird?

554
00:35:56,511 --> 00:36:01,034
No one asks who I am
or why I'm co-directing this.

555
00:36:04,490 --> 00:36:06,443
Why do you think?

556
00:36:12,389 --> 00:36:14,220
Yi Jae.

557
00:36:14,220 --> 00:36:16,202
Ju Yi Jae!

558
00:36:27,868 --> 00:36:30,906
Why am I crying?

559
00:36:30,906 --> 00:36:33,738
I didn't even cry when I won the Grand Prize.

560
00:36:36,365 --> 00:36:39,014
Why is this so sad?

561
00:36:44,855 --> 00:36:48,057
[Gyeongseong Love Song]
But do things like this sell these days?

562
00:36:49,742 --> 00:36:50,977
Ma'am.

563
00:36:50,977 --> 00:36:52,352
Yes?

564
00:36:53,362 --> 00:36:55,372
The car is ready.

565
00:36:56,504 --> 00:36:58,947
How do I look today?

566
00:36:58,947 --> 00:37:00,288
Were you yawning?

567
00:37:00,288 --> 00:37:01,977
Darn it.

568
00:37:04,142 --> 00:37:05,984
Look closer.

569
00:37:06,945 --> 00:37:08,779
Forget it. Just give me the contract.

570
00:37:08,779 --> 00:37:09,974
Yes, ma'am.

571
00:37:11,905 --> 00:37:15,651
It's been a while. I'm kind of excited.

572
00:37:15,651 --> 00:37:17,446
- Let's go!
- Okay.

573
00:37:26,427 --> 00:37:28,075
- Let's go.
- Yes.

574
00:37:42,151 --> 00:37:45,057
Looks like she's leaving now.

575
00:37:45,057 --> 00:37:46,650
Okay.

576
00:38:18,481 --> 00:38:19,988
[Oh Ha Na]

577
00:38:30,413 --> 00:38:32,256
[Contract for Pop Culture Artists]

578
00:38:49,595 --> 00:38:51,270
[Gyeongseong Love Song]

579
00:38:52,035 --> 00:38:54,182
"Gyeongseong Love Song?"

580
00:39:10,831 --> 00:39:15,228
"A single ray of moonlight
falls over Wolhajeong.

581
00:39:15,228 --> 00:39:19,019
Nan Young stands in the heart of the darkness."

582
00:39:28,401 --> 00:39:30,281
Nan Young.

583
00:39:30,281 --> 00:39:35,292
After catching her breath,
she sets down the heavy bag in her hand

584
00:39:35,292 --> 00:39:37,725
and takes something out.

585
00:39:38,517 --> 00:39:42,585
In her trembling hand is a stick of dynamite.

586
00:39:45,170 --> 00:39:47,609
Her mind is already made up.

587
00:39:48,249 --> 00:39:51,155
The moment she lights this fuse,

588
00:39:51,945 --> 00:39:54,639
everything will begin.

589
00:39:57,372 --> 00:40:00,962
After hiding explosives all over Wolhajeong,

590
00:40:00,962 --> 00:40:03,645
she stands there, gripping the fuse tight.

591
00:40:04,298 --> 00:40:09,948
Below the wall,
her face flickers red in the match light.

592
00:40:15,372 --> 00:40:19,757
Tonight, she will blow up Wolhajeong.

593
00:40:20,819 --> 00:40:22,429
<i>Now I finally understand.</i>

594
00:40:22,429 --> 00:40:26,506
<i>Wolhajeong's high walls
were never fences that protected me.</i>

595
00:40:26,506 --> 00:40:29,646
<i>They were bars that kept me locked away.</i>

596
00:40:29,646 --> 00:40:33,466
<i>Now, with my own hands,
I will tear it all down.</i>

597
00:40:49,959 --> 00:40:52,023
Let's go.

598
00:40:57,645 --> 00:41:00,877
<i>I found my way out.</i>

599
00:41:04,191 --> 00:41:06,327
Make yourself comfortable.

600
00:41:08,811 --> 00:41:12,490
No, it's okay.

601
00:41:14,968 --> 00:41:16,535
So...

602
00:41:17,742 --> 00:41:19,867
Have you decided?

603
00:41:20,629 --> 00:41:23,079
I'm not a patient woman.

604
00:41:23,902 --> 00:41:28,006
I want to make it, CEO An.

605
00:41:29,842 --> 00:41:31,866
Can that happen...

606
00:41:33,039 --> 00:41:34,741
in a month?

607
00:41:37,307 --> 00:41:39,791
I told you, I'm impatient.

608
00:41:43,097 --> 00:41:45,979
[Contract for Pop Culture Artists]

609
00:41:59,403 --> 00:42:01,789
How does it feel today?

610
00:42:02,903 --> 00:42:07,068
It feels real, but also like a dream.

611
00:42:08,076 --> 00:42:13,278
But it's our first crew dinner,
and In Uk still didn't show.

612
00:42:13,278 --> 00:42:15,751
He has a dating show today.

613
00:42:15,751 --> 00:42:18,616
- A dating show?
- A romance reality show.

614
00:42:20,105 --> 00:42:22,689
What is he even doing?

615
00:42:22,689 --> 00:42:25,984
Well, as long as we have the company card.

616
00:42:25,984 --> 00:42:29,106
He said you'd be paying.

617
00:42:29,106 --> 00:42:32,745
- Me?
- He said to keep the receipts.

618
00:42:32,745 --> 00:42:35,727
Is he trying to ruin my credit?

619
00:42:37,592 --> 00:42:39,838
There's Director Ju.

620
00:42:41,238 --> 00:42:42,976
- Hello.
- Oh, hi.

621
00:42:42,976 --> 00:42:44,813
- Hello.
- Hello.

622
00:42:44,813 --> 00:42:46,921
- You're here.
- Hello.

623
00:43:10,669 --> 00:43:13,793
Director Seo is shooting on the island, right?

624
00:43:13,793 --> 00:43:15,333
Isn't that close?

625
00:43:15,333 --> 00:43:19,323
Don't even think about going.
It's a mess over there.

626
00:43:19,323 --> 00:43:22,127
One wrong move, and you're stuck there too.

627
00:43:22,127 --> 00:43:27,379
It's basically a prison camp.
The crew's ready to build a raft and escape.

628
00:43:27,379 --> 00:43:30,504
You mean Director Seo Dong Yun?

629
00:43:30,504 --> 00:43:33,138
He's famous for being strict.

630
00:43:33,138 --> 00:43:37,138
I heard his sets
are some of the toughest around.

631
00:43:40,495 --> 00:43:42,185
Director Ju.

632
00:43:42,185 --> 00:43:44,932
I guess you're not tough.

633
00:43:44,932 --> 00:43:48,077
Directors are supposed to be strict.

634
00:43:48,077 --> 00:43:50,704
That's how Director Seo got this far.

635
00:43:50,704 --> 00:43:55,096
Anyone who survives that set
wears it like a badge.

636
00:43:55,096 --> 00:43:58,104
Right. It becomes pride.

637
00:43:59,086 --> 00:44:02,216
Art Director, there you are.

638
00:44:02,216 --> 00:44:05,433
Why are you sitting here?

639
00:44:05,433 --> 00:44:08,407
You went to Seonghwa Arts College, right?

640
00:44:08,407 --> 00:44:10,715
Can I call you senior?

641
00:44:10,715 --> 00:44:13,036
Just call me Se Ra.

642
00:44:13,036 --> 00:44:14,493
Yes, Se Ra.

643
00:44:14,493 --> 00:44:18,346
I'm Ryu Sang Mok,
Seonghwa Theater and Film, class of '02.

644
00:44:18,346 --> 00:44:20,370
I was never that attached to my school.

645
00:44:20,370 --> 00:44:23,276
Then get attached to me.

646
00:44:23,276 --> 00:44:25,228
- Excuse me!
- Huh?

647
00:44:25,228 --> 00:44:28,108
Who are you talking to?

648
00:44:37,000 --> 00:44:39,071
Director Ju.

649
00:44:39,766 --> 00:44:42,109
Where did you go to college?

650
00:44:42,998 --> 00:44:47,627
Why did you become a reporter
instead of using your major?

651
00:44:49,299 --> 00:44:51,766
- I...
- Cheers!

652
00:44:53,122 --> 00:44:54,553
Raise your glass.

653
00:44:54,553 --> 00:44:56,694
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

654
00:45:07,176 --> 00:45:10,559
Is life seriously this unfair?

655
00:45:10,559 --> 00:45:12,229
Tell me about it.

656
00:45:12,229 --> 00:45:16,522
Some people grind for 13 years
and still never debut.

657
00:45:16,522 --> 00:45:19,247
Hey, Mr. Five Years.

658
00:45:19,247 --> 00:45:21,981
That number was pretty specific.

659
00:45:21,981 --> 00:45:23,579
Are you talking about me?

660
00:45:23,579 --> 00:45:28,414
I mean, with veterans like you still waiting...

661
00:45:28,414 --> 00:45:31,532
- And some total nobody... huh?
- Yeah.

662
00:45:31,532 --> 00:45:33,725
Exactly.

663
00:45:33,725 --> 00:45:36,245
Darn it.

664
00:45:37,068 --> 00:45:39,046
I need to pee.

665
00:45:40,778 --> 00:45:43,415
But this is too much!

666
00:45:43,415 --> 00:45:46,336
She's a former reporter.

667
00:45:46,336 --> 00:45:49,334
Fine. I can let that slide.

668
00:45:49,334 --> 00:45:50,638
But what?

669
00:45:50,638 --> 00:45:52,482
She's never even studied film.

670
00:45:52,482 --> 00:45:56,414
Plenty of directors didn't study film.

671
00:45:56,414 --> 00:45:58,438
Come on!

672
00:45:58,438 --> 00:46:01,546
There are levels to that.

673
00:46:01,546 --> 00:46:06,346
It's not like she went
to Korea University or Harvard.

674
00:46:06,346 --> 00:46:09,916
How does some no-name college grad
just waltz in?

675
00:46:09,916 --> 00:46:11,276
Calm down.

676
00:46:11,276 --> 00:46:14,213
What's taking so long? Huh?

677
00:46:14,213 --> 00:46:18,838
- Calm down.
- I'll kick this door down.

678
00:46:20,135 --> 00:46:21,549
- No, no.
- Darn it.

679
00:46:21,549 --> 00:46:23,651
Calm down.

680
00:46:25,638 --> 00:46:27,348
Hey! Come out already!

681
00:46:27,348 --> 00:46:30,507
- Hold on.
- Come out! Hey!

682
00:46:30,507 --> 00:46:32,454
- Calm down.
- Do you know who I am?

683
00:46:32,454 --> 00:46:35,067
- Calm down, sir.
- What the...

684
00:46:35,067 --> 00:46:37,235
I'm sorry.

685
00:46:37,235 --> 00:46:39,161
Director Ju?

686
00:46:49,581 --> 00:46:52,376
She heard you! Jeez...

687
00:46:52,376 --> 00:46:54,210
It's true, though!

688
00:46:54,210 --> 00:46:56,263
- Yi Jae.
- You need the bathroom?

689
00:46:56,263 --> 00:46:58,307
Someone's in there.

690
00:46:58,990 --> 00:47:01,009
I'm saying it loud so she hears me!

691
00:47:01,009 --> 00:47:05,889
I studied film! She didn't even major in it...

692
00:47:05,889 --> 00:47:09,265
- I want to be a director too!
- Stop it.

693
00:47:09,265 --> 00:47:14,079
It's my first time, so please help me a lot.

694
00:47:14,079 --> 00:47:16,256
I look forward to working with you.

695
00:47:16,256 --> 00:47:18,571
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

696
00:47:22,948 --> 00:47:24,127
Try this.

697
00:47:24,127 --> 00:47:27,480
Director Woo, come have a drink.

698
00:47:30,517 --> 00:47:32,802
Here, sir.

699
00:47:45,962 --> 00:47:47,679
I'll get going first.

700
00:47:47,679 --> 00:47:50,058
Are you going home? Should I drive you?

701
00:47:50,058 --> 00:47:51,379
I'll take a cab.

702
00:47:51,379 --> 00:47:53,734
Okay. Get home safe.

703
00:47:53,734 --> 00:47:56,467
- Good night.
- Good night.

704
00:47:56,467 --> 00:47:59,417
- Then we'll...
- Where are you going?

705
00:47:59,417 --> 00:48:01,724
Round two!

706
00:48:01,724 --> 00:48:03,780
Round two!

707
00:48:03,780 --> 00:48:05,490
- Round two!
- Oh my...

708
00:48:05,490 --> 00:48:07,087
Round two!

709
00:48:10,016 --> 00:48:12,016
[Jinsusungchan]

710
00:48:24,795 --> 00:48:26,617
When...

711
00:48:26,617 --> 00:48:27,788
When did you get here?

712
00:48:27,788 --> 00:48:29,680
- Director Ryu.
- Yes?

713
00:48:29,680 --> 00:48:34,177
This is the first and last time
I'll explain my decision.

714
00:48:34,177 --> 00:48:35,627
Sorry?

715
00:48:35,627 --> 00:48:37,818
What do you mean?

716
00:48:37,818 --> 00:48:41,259
"Gyeongseong Love Song" was written
by Yi Jae in her senior year.

717
00:48:41,259 --> 00:48:45,097
That's why I left the script meeting
entirely to her.

718
00:48:45,097 --> 00:48:49,390
I decided it made more sense for me
to handle location scouting.

719
00:48:50,560 --> 00:48:52,197
Director Ryu.

720
00:48:52,197 --> 00:48:56,378
Director Ju Yi Jae is doing her job perfectly.

721
00:48:58,607 --> 00:48:59,625
Yeah...

722
00:48:59,625 --> 00:49:02,194
Does even hearing that bother you?

723
00:49:02,194 --> 00:49:04,087
Not at all.

724
00:49:04,701 --> 00:49:07,557
Absolutely not.

725
00:49:07,557 --> 00:49:09,854
I'm sorry.

726
00:49:09,854 --> 00:49:12,308
You don't need to apologize to me.

727
00:49:12,921 --> 00:49:15,455
From now on,

728
00:49:15,455 --> 00:49:19,253
let's each do our part and respect each other.

729
00:49:19,253 --> 00:49:20,343
Got it.

730
00:49:20,343 --> 00:49:22,047
Enjoy your meal.

731
00:49:25,704 --> 00:49:27,235
Hey.

732
00:49:28,231 --> 00:49:29,241
Ma'am.

733
00:49:29,241 --> 00:49:31,442
Please put the staff meals on my card.

734
00:49:31,442 --> 00:49:33,817
You're paying for all of them?

735
00:50:01,558 --> 00:50:02,782
<i>No.</i>

736
00:50:02,782 --> 00:50:04,950
<i>Nobody said anything.</i>

737
00:50:04,950 --> 00:50:07,116
<i>Isn't that weird?</i>

738
00:50:07,116 --> 00:50:11,822
<i>No one asks who I am
or why I'm co-directing this.</i>

739
00:50:11,822 --> 00:50:13,826
<i>It's true, though!</i>

740
00:50:13,826 --> 00:50:15,628
<i>Calm down...</i>

741
00:50:18,665 --> 00:50:20,644
<i>I'm saying it loud so she hears me!</i>

742
00:50:20,644 --> 00:50:23,345
<i>I studied film! She didn't even...</i>

743
00:50:31,209 --> 00:50:33,019
- Hello?
<i>- Where are you?</i>

744
00:50:33,019 --> 00:50:35,043
<i>We need to talk.</i>

745
00:50:35,043 --> 00:50:37,067
I'm outside your place.

746
00:50:37,067 --> 00:50:39,380
[Jaejae Noodles]

747
00:50:50,361 --> 00:50:52,032
What are you doing?

748
00:50:52,696 --> 00:50:54,261
Watch me.

749
00:50:55,085 --> 00:50:57,831
- Why are you...
- Just watch from there!

750
00:51:02,076 --> 00:51:03,146
See?

751
00:51:03,146 --> 00:51:04,903
I can run like this!

752
00:51:04,903 --> 00:51:07,102
It doesn't hurt at all!

753
00:52:27,917 --> 00:52:33,138
<i>You know how I've lived.</i>

754
00:52:35,007 --> 00:52:39,367
<i>I spent whole days stuck in mudflats.</i>

755
00:52:40,374 --> 00:52:43,417
<i>I climbed countless mountains.</i>

756
00:53:00,214 --> 00:53:02,373
So stop.

757
00:53:03,675 --> 00:53:09,430
Because of you, my scar feels even clearer.

758
00:53:14,398 --> 00:53:17,914
If you're truly sorry,

759
00:53:17,914 --> 00:53:20,604
if you feel that bad for me,

760
00:53:22,344 --> 00:53:25,280
then see this too.

761
00:53:26,054 --> 00:53:29,003
Even after everything, I'm standing here now.

762
00:53:31,188 --> 00:53:33,682
Please understand

763
00:53:34,888 --> 00:53:37,444
what it took to get here.

764
00:53:37,444 --> 00:53:39,308
Please.

765
00:53:41,152 --> 00:53:43,576
I really want to do this well.

766
00:53:43,576 --> 00:53:45,847
I don't want any more regrets.

767
00:53:51,466 --> 00:53:53,602
Help me, Soo Bin.

768
00:53:54,643 --> 00:53:57,089
Help me keep running.

769
00:54:00,265 --> 00:54:01,662
<i>What's your dream?</i>

770
00:54:01,662 --> 00:54:03,887
<i>A film director.</i>

771
00:54:03,887 --> 00:54:05,309
<i>Hurry!</i>

772
00:54:06,325 --> 00:54:08,910
<i>Pretty cool, right?</i>

773
00:54:13,751 --> 00:54:18,325
<i>I'll be a director
who makes films that feel human.</i>

774
00:54:18,325 --> 00:54:20,700
<i>Let's go, Ju Yi Jae!</i>

775
00:54:23,013 --> 00:54:26,216
<i>Let's make a movie together.</i>

776
00:54:26,216 --> 00:54:29,709
<i>Let's do something great.</i>

777
00:54:31,933 --> 00:54:33,494
<i>Romance.</i>

778
00:54:33,494 --> 00:54:36,048
<i>Let's write a romance together.</i>

779
00:54:36,048 --> 00:54:38,424
<i>A really great one.</i>

780
00:54:59,809 --> 00:55:02,489
I always wanted to be like you.

781
00:55:03,659 --> 00:55:06,343
That bright look on your face.

782
00:55:17,297 --> 00:55:20,670
That's why I like you, Yi Jae.

783
00:55:42,444 --> 00:55:44,349
This is what I should've done

784
00:55:45,036 --> 00:55:47,314
when we were 19.

785
00:56:05,721 --> 00:56:09,630
I'll stop here.

786
00:56:12,091 --> 00:56:14,576
So you can shine brighter.

787
00:56:15,352 --> 00:56:21,318
I can't be a stain on your life anymore.

788
00:56:21,318 --> 00:56:22,971
I'm sorry.

789
00:56:23,714 --> 00:56:25,345
No.

790
00:56:27,245 --> 00:56:31,022
I wasn't asking for an apology.

791
00:56:31,022 --> 00:56:33,635
I was asking you to help me.

792
00:56:34,246 --> 00:56:36,398
I'm sorry.

793
00:56:37,023 --> 00:56:39,364
This is all I can do.

794
00:56:40,936 --> 00:56:42,874
What matters is...

795
00:56:42,874 --> 00:56:47,291
we finish the movie together.

796
00:56:48,138 --> 00:56:52,141
But give me some time to sort myself out.

797
00:56:55,771 --> 00:56:58,687
Until the new draft is ready,

798
00:56:58,687 --> 00:57:01,857
I'll work alone at home.

799
00:57:01,857 --> 00:57:03,573
Take care.

800
00:57:06,681 --> 00:57:09,827
Why say it like we're saying goodbye forever?

801
00:57:09,827 --> 00:57:12,409
I guess we are.

802
00:57:12,409 --> 00:57:14,173
To our first love.

803
00:57:15,087 --> 00:57:19,695
Once the new draft comes in,
let's meet as colleagues.

804
00:57:21,656 --> 00:57:24,996
Oh, that kind of goodbye...

805
00:57:27,674 --> 00:57:29,647
Okay.

806
00:57:29,647 --> 00:57:31,067
Bye.

807
00:57:31,067 --> 00:57:32,570
Yi Jae.

808
00:57:32,570 --> 00:57:34,303
Yeah.

809
00:57:34,303 --> 00:57:37,322
See you soon, Director Ju.

810
00:57:37,980 --> 00:57:39,643
Bye.

811
00:58:46,801 --> 00:58:48,911
<i>Director Ju.</i>

812
00:58:48,911 --> 00:58:51,625
<i>I really want to be in this film.</i>

813
00:58:51,625 --> 00:58:52,818
<i>Who's coming?</i>

814
00:58:52,818 --> 00:58:53,942
<i>Sim Yu Geon?</i>

815
00:58:53,942 --> 00:58:55,474
<i>- Soo Bin?
- What do you want?</i>

816
00:58:55,474 --> 00:58:58,612
<i>Give him the role, or drop Ju Yi Jae.</i>

817
00:58:58,612 --> 00:59:01,549
<i>I hate when you show up like this.</i>

818
00:59:01,549 --> 00:59:05,333
<i>Amazing! The vibe changed when he walked in.</i>

819
00:59:05,333 --> 00:59:07,759
<i>- Time flies.
- Waiting for you felt longer...</i>

820
00:59:07,759 --> 00:59:09,146
<i>I should go.</i>

821
00:59:09,146 --> 00:59:12,091
<i>Then what were we back then?</i>

822
00:59:12,091 --> 00:59:14,199
<i>I think it's love.</i>

